}

USER:
Today's date: 2026-10-30
Athlete timezone: Europe/Oslo

Athlete profile (answers last saved 2026-10-18):
- What is your main goal?: A 200 km brevet in early April 2027, then the full brevet series toward Paris-Brest-Paris in August 2027.
- How old are you?: 47
- Where do you live?: Trondheim, Norway.
- What is your training history and current performance?: About 3,200 km this year. FTP 225 W, threshold heart rate 160 bpm, easy running around 5:30 per km. I can handle a long ride at the weekend and two hard-ish weekday sessions.
- How much time can you train each week?: Around eight hours. Sixty to ninety minutes on weekday evenings after work, and longer rides at the weekend.
- What is your body weight and body-fat percentage?: 82.0 kg at 24.5 % body fat.
- What is your diet goal?: Get down to 18 % body fat by September 2027 without losing power or muscle.
- What are your constraints and preferences?: Lower back tightness after long rides and saddle discomfort beyond four hours. I will ride in rain, but I stay on the trainer after dark and I avoid ice. I like structure, but I burn out after about four months of disciplined training, so I need variety.
- What equipment can you train on?: Road bike with a power meter, wheel-on indoor trainer, a gym at work, cross-country skis and running shoes.
- Do you have any injuries?: (skipped)

Athlete FTP: 225 W (the latest FTP the athlete stated or the coach estimated as of today). Use this as the baseline for the week-by-week FTP estimate and for TSS.

FTP history (oldest first; "user" and "garmin" values are measurements, "coach" values are earlier estimates):
