1. 2026-10-25 — cycling — Sunday Endurance Ride: 62.00 km, 21.9 km/h, 2:50:00 moving, 820 m elevation, NP 198 W (average 168 W).
   Coach analysis: A well-paced four-hour endurance ride. Normalized power of 198 W is 88 % of FTP, so the aerobic load landed where the week needed it. The last hour cost more than the first two because the climbs were ridden above the plan; keep the same duration next weekend but cap the climbs.
   Athlete comment about this same activity (not an additional session): Felt strong until the last hour, when my lower back tightened on the climbs.
   Coach reply to that comment: That is a solid ride. Next time keep the climbs two gears easier: you get the same aerobic benefit without spending the last hour paying for it.
