   Strength sets: Squat: 1 × 10 reps at 16 kg; Deadlift: 1 × 8 reps at 60 kg
   Coach analysis: A controlled strength session. The goblet squats at 16 kg and the trap-bar pull at 60 kg were both inside the prescribed effort, so the load is right to repeat before adding weight.
3. 2026-10-23 — running — Easy Run: 8.10 km, 5:33 /km, 45:00 moving, 60 m elevation.
   Coach analysis: An easy 5:33 per km run, close to the athlete's conversational pace. Heart rate stayed low, so this is useful running durability without adding meaningful fatigue before the weekend.
4. 2026-10-22 — cycling — Trainer Sweet Spot: 40.00 km, 32.0 km/h, 1:15:00 moving, NP 228 W (average 205 W).
   Coach analysis: Three sweet-spot blocks at 228 W normalized, just above the prescribed 88 % of FTP. The third block held its power, so the session did its job; the cadence stayed above 85 rpm throughout.
5. 2026-10-20 — cycling — Recovery Spin: 28.00 km, 28.1 km/h, 1:00:00 moving, 190 m elevation, NP 130 W (average 118 W).
   Coach analysis: An easy hour at 118 W average. That is genuine recovery work: it moved the legs without adding load, which is what the day after a weekend ride needs.
6. 2026-10-18 — hiking — Bymarka Hike: 11.00 km, 12:15 /km, 2:15:00 moving, 320 m elevation.
   Coach analysis: An eleven-kilometre hike with 320 m of climbing. The effort stayed aerobic and the ankles had no reaction, so hiking remains a good low-impact weekend option while the weather holds.

