Current season plan:
Goal: Complete the 2027 brevet series and Paris-Brest-Paris comfortably, while losing body fat without losing power.
Dates: 2026-10-19 → 2027-04-04 — estimated FTP 225 W
Rationale: The season is aerobic-first: a long base that uses the trainer, skiing and hiking to build durability through a Norwegian winter, then a sustained-power build and a brevet-specific block, with a two-week taper into the April 200 km event. Keeping the hard work in short, varied doses protects against the burnout the athlete describes after four disciplined months.
Blocks:
1. Aerobic Base and Strength Foundation (2026-10-19 → 2026-12-06, 7 weeks): Build aerobic durability, efficient cadence and low-load strength without stacking fatigue.
2. Winter Build and Cross-Training (2026-12-07 → 2027-01-17, 6 weeks): Hold cycling specificity through controlled threshold work while skiing and easy running carry the aerobic load.
3. Endurance and Sustained-Power Build (2027-01-18 → 2027-02-28, 6 weeks): Progress sustained threshold power, long weekend endurance and fuelling practice across late winter and early spring.
4. Brevet-Specific Preparation (2027-03-01 → 2027-03-21, 3 weeks): Convert fitness into 200 km durability with conservative pacing, fuelling and back-to-back weekend riding.
5. Taper and Race Readiness (2027-03-22 → 2027-04-04, 2 weeks): Reduce volume while keeping one brief opener, then arrive at the brevet fresh and fuelled.

Current block plan:
Block: Aerobic Base and Strength Foundation
Focus: Build aerobic durability, efficient cadence and low-load strength without stacking fatigue.
Dates: 2026-10-19 → 2026-12-06 — estimated FTP 225 W
Rationale: Seven weeks of consistent aerobic work with two short strength sessions, a growing weekend ride and one controlled sweet-spot session a week once the rhythm is established. Volume rises for three weeks, holds for two, then deloads before the winter block, so the athlete absorbs the load instead of arriving at December tired.
Weeks:
- Week 1 (from 2026-10-19): Restore the weekly rhythm with easy aerobic work and two short strength sessions; target load: 5.0-5.5 hours; about 230 TSS; estimated FTP 225 W
- Week 2 (from 2026-10-26): Hold the rhythm and add one controlled sweet-spot session on the trainer; target load: 6.0-6.5 hours; about 290 TSS; estimated FTP 225 W
- Week 3 (from 2026-11-02): Extend the weekend ride and keep every aerobic effort under the heart-rate cap; target load: 6.5-7.0 hours; about 320 TSS; estimated FTP 226 W
- Week 4 (from 2026-11-09): Peak block volume with one longer endurance ride and steady strength loads; target load: 7.0-7.5 hours; about 350 TSS; estimated FTP 227 W
- Week 5 (from 2026-11-16): Consolidate the aerobic base and test cadence discipline on the trainer; target load: 6.5-7.0 hours; about 310 TSS; estimated FTP 227 W
- Week 6 (from 2026-11-23): Deload week: cut volume by a quarter and keep the strength sessions short; target load: 4.5-5.0 hours; about 210 TSS; estimated FTP 226 W
- Week 7 (from 2026-11-30): Finish the block with an easy long ride and head into winter training fresh; target load: 5.5-6.0 hours; about 260 TSS; estimated FTP 227 W

